00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:53.120
Banks are an influential and vital part of the modern-day economy

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.040
They provide various banking services to the general public,

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.560
issue loans and create liquidity in markets. Moreover, they

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:04.800
provide other financial services such as currency exchange and certificates of safe deposits...etc.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:12.080
In short, banks are the safest places to keep money in today's world with all its risks and complexities.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:17.160
But these same banks may be in real trouble if there are problems in the economy of their countries.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:23.040
The extent of its predicament varies according to how profound are the problems and crises that its country's economy is going through.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:27.080
This situation may result in one or more banks going bankrupt.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:31.440
A serious problem related to the lot of depositors' money rises here.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.120
This is the question that concerns everyone, without exception, when a bank goes bankrupt

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:39.600
As for savings accounts, certificates, and all other forms of depositing

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.240
which customer or depositor adopt, what will their status be in this case?

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.880
So, before you question the current situation of the bank you are dealing with;

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:51.240
let me first highlight when exactly a bank goes bankrupt and how?

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:56.480
When you go to a bank to deposit money, or else, when some money is transferred to your account:

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:01.360
the bank keeps a very small part of this money and the rest is invested.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.040
Banks in this case are more like a recruitment company

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:09.080
On one hand, it takes your money and invests it; on the other hand you get an interest in exchange for it.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:12.880
So, what is the amount of money that the banks must keep, roughly?

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:18.480
The entity that determines this ratio, which is called the “Reserve Requirement”, is the central bank of the state

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.400
Its authority is to oversee the commercial banking system

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.680
within its country through supervisory and regulatory powers.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.245
What is meant by ‘Reserve Requirement’?

00:05:25.245 --> 00:05:28.400
It is a percentage of the total funds of depositors in banks,

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.800
whether they are in local or foreign currencies,

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.360
a percentage that every commercial bank must keep in an

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:38.440
account with the Central Bank without any interest or fees from the Central Bank in return.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.480
One of the main goals of reserve requirements is to prevent a bank

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:46.840
from ceasing to function if unexpected large mass withdrawals occur.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:51.360
For example, if we look at Egyptian banks, we will find that the Central Bank of Egypt

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.089
imposed a reserve requirement ratio of 14% on each bank,

00:05:53.089 --> 00:06:02.400
this ratio was 10% until October 2017 but the Central Bank raised it to 14% now.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:07.200
For example, if I deposited 100,000 L.E by tomorrow at any bank in Egypt;

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:13.080
this bank must hold 14,000 pounds of the total sum in its account at the Egyptian Central Bank

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:17.440
According to the statistical bulletin of the Central Bank issued last February,

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:22.640
the total deposits of the banking sector in Egypt, by the end of December for the year 2021,

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:26.680
amounted to 6.4 trillion pounds which means that 14% of that

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:30.400
sum is commercial bank's reserve at Egypt's Central Bank.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.840
Of course, this ratio differs from one country to another.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:36.720
There are countries that do not require a reserve for commercial banks at all,

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.320
such as Canada, the United Kingdom and New Zealand.

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:42.000
Hence, how does the bank deal with the rest of that sum of money?

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.760
Of course, banks do not save it in their vaults. they would rather

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:48.920
invest it so that you can pay back the deposits interests and make some profits.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:53.120
The simplest form of investment is to provide loans to customers,

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:56.160
whether they are individuals, companies, or the government itself.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.200
There are other, more complex investment methods, such as

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:03.800
buying shares in the stock exchange, buying certain assets such as lands and real estate,

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:08.600
or acquiring certain profitable projects, and other different forms of investment.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:13.440
Banks here, like any investor, are subject to loss when

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:18.280
the economic situation is distressed or the economy is experiencing exact difficulties.

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:22.840
Therefore a bank’s investments can be lost and a calamity breaks out.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:27.880
When a bank realizes losses, it will be unable to fulfill its obligations towards its depositors and creditors.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:33.440
It consequently cannot neither provide cash to depositors, nor commit to its obligations to creditors.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.120
Hence, the value of its assets falls below the market value of its obligations.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:43.200
For example, if the sum of deposits in a bank reaches 10 billion dollars

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:47.760
and the bank loses large sums of money in some investments.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:51.080
Its assets will be decreased as a result down to 5-7 billion dollars.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:54.360
Here the bank will declare bankruptcy. It is possible for banks to go bankrupt due to

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:58.600
financial chaos and economic collapse accompanied by high levels of corruption,

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:03.720
as the situation in Lebanon currently, wherein banks are looting depositors’ money.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:06.200
Coming to another more important question: What happens when

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:09.160
bankruptcy occurs and the bank liabilities are greater than its assets?

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:11.680
The biggest problem of a bank at such a time is that

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:16.000
the depositors get to know that the bank is insolvent and is no longer able to pay them.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.640
In this case, the bank probably borrows from other banks

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:22.560
which is in their interest to keep the insolvent bank steadfast.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:27.280
Questioning why? Because as soon as depositors get to know that the bank is insolvent,

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:30.480
a bank-run would take place wherein clients would be withdrawing their money.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:34.560
If this happened, it would be a disaster. Bank panic will arise and

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:37.082
people will run to banks to withdraw their deposits, including

00:08:37.082 --> 00:08:40.400
those banks that are in sound condition even . This will reduce

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:43.080
the liquidity of the insolvent bank more than it is.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:48.000
So, the insolvent bank will be forced to stop the withdrawals or

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.080
set limits by allowing the withdrawal of only small amounts.

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:55.600
People's main concern in such a case is to know what is going to happen to their money in that bank.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.240
Will they be able to get it back or not?

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:05.800
A model of significance in the United States can be taken into consideration before discussing the destiny of depositors’ money in banks that can go bankrupt in some Arab countries.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:10.120
Let's go back to the twenties of the last century, to the beginning of the Great Depression,

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:13.840
many banks were bankrupting on a daily basis in the US.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:18.640
depositors lost their money and there was no way to recover it back.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:23.000
Can you imagine that a third of American banks declared bankruptcy at that time!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:29.840
From 1929 to 1933, a total of 10,000 American banks had declared bankruptcy.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.760
American depositors' money had been gone forever.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:37.600
They lost 140 billion dollars in this short period due to bank failure.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:42.240
This led to depositors running to all banks to withdraw their deposits at the same time,

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:49.440
there was not enough money in vaults because banks invest most of the money they get as aforementioned.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:54.840
In the midst of this financial collapse, US President Franklin Roosevelt signed the Banking Act,

00:09:54.840 --> 00:10:06.240
known as the Glass-Steagall Act of 1933, to establish the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation, known for short, FDIC.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:09.560
The mission of this institution at the time was to restore the confidence

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:13.600
of panicked Americans in the banking sector in the wake of this financial collapse,

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:18.000
thus the institution would serve as a bulwark against bank panic in the future.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:21.640
So, what is the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation job?

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.880
It protects customers’ deposits in the cases of bankruptcy or failure of any of

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:28.600
the commercial banks insured only by the institution (the insurance is optional for the banks)

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:34.760
There are banks that do not want to be insured. By the way,

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:39.240
if you are in the United States, you must make sure that the bank in which you are depositing your money

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:43.880
is insured by the FDIC, otherwise your savings will be in greater danger than if you put them in an insured bank.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:47.560
Regarding the insurance of the depositors’ money; a point of significance pops up here:

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:52.160
the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation does not return all deposits if

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:56.880
the bank falters or fails as it covers a maximum of 250 thousand

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:00.000
dollars per account in each single bank. To make it clear; if someone

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.400
opened a bank account; and deposited 350 thousand dollars;

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.200
the maximum sum of money that person would get back if the bank falters or fails is only 250 thousand.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:11.240
As for the remaining 100,000, you will wait for

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:14.080
the liquidation of the bank’s assets or the sale of the entire bank.

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:15.240
Then, they may be / may be NOT able to get the money back.

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:18.880
Some details worth mentioning at this stance; you can process your accounts

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:22.440
to be fully insured with more than 250 thousand dollars.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:28.160
For example, distributing your savings to different banks in case the sum is more than 250,000 $

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:31.040
because the insurance limits include each single bank.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.808
Otherwise, you can open specific accounts (not individual accounts), such as a joint account

00:11:32.808 --> 00:11:38.160
in which there is a beneficiary; or certain types of accounts Like retirement accounts.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:42.320
Some people may think that it is unlikely that a bank is going bankrupt in America now;

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:48.320
as the last crystal clear bankruptcies were during the global financial crisis in 2008 -2009.

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:58.360
Not true! In the last 15 years, almost every year, banks falter and fail in the US, except for 2018 and 2021.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:01.520
The number is much less than the days of the financial crisis of course

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:07.520
but there are still faltering banks and the Deposit Insurance Corporation undertaking their settlement.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:11.920
If we look at the last five years, we will see that in 2017, eight

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:15.840
American banks failed with total assets of about 6.5 billion dollars.

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:21.240
In 2018, no banks failed. Yet in 2019, four banks failed

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:25.560
with a total assets of 214 million dollars. In 2020,

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:30.720
four banks failed with total assets of 458 million dollars

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:37.600
among which is the Almena State Bank in Kansas, which stumbled on October 23, 2020.

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:41.160
Since then no other banks have stumbled in the United States.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:47.200
Here in the Middle East, there are central banks that guarantee depositors’ money, either fully or partially.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:50.440
However, there are other central banks that do not offer this type of insurance

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:55.560
Yet, even if the central bank of your country, whatever it is, does not insure deposits;

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:01.840
as it works carefully not to expose the depositors sums of money to risk from the early beginning.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:07.040
Any central bank uses its supervisory and regulatory powers to ensure the member banks

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:12.480
do not engage in any activity that could be unstable or put depositors' money at risk.

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:16.560
Well, let's suppose that a bank for any reason is bankrupt.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:21.000
What is the fate of that one that goes bankrupt? What is its eventuality?

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:25.480
The central bank is often the institution specialized with settling troubled banks.

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:29.200
Nonetheless, the US Federal Reserve is not responsible for this issue in the US.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:33.080
As I said before, the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:36.680
is the one that takes charge of matters for any bankrupt bank.

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:40.600
So, the first thing the Central Bank or this Deposit Insurance Corporation

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:45.080
does is to contract with another bank or rent another sound bank with sound management

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:48.880
and let it take over the office of the failed or faltering bank until

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:53.400
it is sold or until its assets go into liquidation if there is no buyer

00:13:53.400 --> 00:14:00.040
The new bank that manages this troubled bank temporarily is called ‘bridge bank’

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:05.320
It takes over all the assets and liabilities of the troubled one and begins to administer it again.

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:10.400
The goal of the bridge bank is to make a restart to this failed bank with its available capabilities

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:14.080
It calms the creditors and depositors down; thus avoiding

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:17.600
a bank panic that could lead to the other banks to fall.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:20.880
That is why its role at such a time is excessively critical and vital

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:24.040
in order to save the economy and prevent a financial collapse.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:27.360
After the bridge bank begins managing the troubled bank,

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:27.860
It takes time until any entity shows up to take over this failed bank.

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:38.640
Sometimes the bridge bank is the one who takes it over. Other times this failed bank is merged with another bank.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:43.080
But, if none of this happened as no one may be courged to take over that troubled bank

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:47.920
a single option is left for the Central Bank to settle the troubled bank:

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.680
which is liquidating its assets.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:54.200
First, an Asset Valuation Review takes place,

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.760
a process in which the value of the troubled bank’s assets is assessed.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:02.240
Thus the appropriate price that the Central Bank or the Deposit Insurance

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:04.720
Corporation will accept to sell the assets at is determined.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:08.560
These assets could be the loans that the faltering bank had at the beginning,

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:13.080
the depositors’ liquid money that was left in the vaults, lands, properties, and others.

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:15.800
After reviewing the assessment of the assets, the sale will be done.

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:21.000
The profit hence is hoped to be distributed between depositors and creditors according to certain accounts and ratios.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:25.440
Back to Lebanon, unfortunately the situation there is unmanageable.

